   A["Program Running"] --> B["User presses Ctrl+C"]
   B --> C["Operating System sends SIGINT"]
   C --> D["Program pauses main task"]
   D --> E["Signal Handler executes cleanup"]
   E --> F["Program exits safely"]
```

## Example from Class
While not in your provided text, in C, you typically use the `<signal.h>` library to handle this. You would use a function called `signal()` to link the `SIGINT` signal to your custom function:

```c
#include <signal.h>

// This is the function that runs when Ctrl+C is pressed
void handle_sigint(int sig) {
    printf("Caught the signal! Cleaning up...\n");
    exit(0);
}

int main() {
    // Tell the system to use our function when SIGINT happens
    signal(SIGINT, handle_sigint);

    // Program logic goes here...
    return 0;
}
```

