## Use Cases
Control flow is used whenever a program needs to make a decision based on data. For example, you use it to check if a user's password is correct, to determine if a game character has enough health to survive an attack, or to decide which menu option a user has selected. Without control flow, programs would be static and unable to interact with the world around them.

